(2686563, 367414, 54917, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by levyj413:</b></div><hr/><i> Wow.  The horns blend perfectly into the stone.  Was that just a lucky coincidence, or were you trying to get that angle?  Or did you change the color in post-processing? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>No colour change, the horns and stone really were like that. A definite slice of luck though as I didn''t realise just how similar they were until I got the shot onto PC. Think the way the light fell on the rocks didn''t do any harm either.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-08-02 01:36:48.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by levyj413: Wow.  The horns blend perfectly into the stone.  Was that just a lucky coincidence, or were you trying to get that angle?  Or did you change the color in post-processing?   No colour change, the horns and stone really were like that. A definite slice of luck though as I didn''t realise just how similar they were until I got the shot onto PC. Think the way the light fell on the rocks didn''t do any harm either.', '2006-08-02 02:29:42.000000', '2006-08-02 02:36:48.000000', 0),
