(2687171, 369132, 52549, '<td valign="top">Beautiful colour tones. Huge congrats on your 5th place.</td>', 'Beautiful colour tones. Huge congrats on your 5th place.', '2006-08-02 05:48:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687172, 369536, 24694, '<td valign="top">I thought you deserved much better on this one. I think it''s fairly obvious why you entered it for ''color on color''. I really think it''s a shame it didn''t get more credit.</td>', 'I thought you deserved much better on this one. I think it''s fairly obvious why you entered it for ''color on color''. I really think it''s a shame it didn''t get more credit.', '2006-08-02 05:49:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687174, 369717, 52549, '<td valign="top">I''m so pleased that this beauty made the top 20. Congratulations.</td>', 'I''m so pleased that this beauty made the top 20. Congratulations.', '2006-08-02 05:49:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687236, 367973, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 9.  Good meet of the Challenge.  Nice composition and good focus.</td>', 'I gave this a 9.  Good meet of the Challenge.  Nice composition and good focus.', '2006-08-02 06:38:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687237, 367855, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8.  Very good detail and color in the petals.  The cherries matched well too, just wish they were a little more dominant ''somehow''.</td>', 'I gave this an 8.  Very good detail and color in the petals.  The cherries matched well too, just wish they were a little more dominant ''somehow''.', '2006-08-02 06:38:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687238, 367682, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8.  Really liked the composition.  Good capture.  Focus looks near perfect.  Only real thing was the change of color/green at the fore, which works well in with the other colors/pads, but if the focus were a little sharper (difficult I realize), may have given this even more of an edge in my opinion.</td>', 'I gave this an 8.  Really liked the composition.  Good capture.  Focus looks near perfect.  Only real thing was the change of color/green at the fore, which works well in with the other colors/pads, but if the focus were a little sharper (difficult I realize), may have given this even more of an edge in my opinion.', '2006-08-02 06:38:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687239, 367622, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8.  Really liked the colors and use of shallow dof.  Composition very good too.  The detail and lines in the leaf upper left is very nice, difficult, but just like to have seen at least the same type of definition on the eyes &amp;/or ''snout'' of the frog.</td>', 'I gave this an 8.  Really liked the colors and use of shallow dof.  Composition very good too.  The detail and lines in the leaf upper left is very nice, difficult, but just like to have seen at least the same type of definition on the eyes &/or ''snout'' of the frog.', '2006-08-02 06:38:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687240, 367856, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8.  Really liked the concept and use of combination of colors.  The main detractor in my opinion was the fact that the paper/cards dominated slightly more than the blueberries.</td>', 'I gave this an 8.  Really liked the concept and use of combination of colors.  The main detractor in my opinion was the fact that the paper/cards dominated slightly more than the blueberries.', '2006-08-02 06:38:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687241, 368205, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8.  Really liked the concept - difficult given the colorings, however just wish the blacks were bolder/more ''depth'', if that makes sense.  Perhaps a variation in lighting, not sure.  Also, just a little sharper on the olives/texture(s).</td>', 'I gave this an 8.  Really liked the concept - difficult given the colorings, however just wish the blacks were bolder/more ''depth'', if that makes sense.  Perhaps a variation in lighting, not sure.  Also, just a little sharper on the olives/texture(s).', '2006-08-02 06:38:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687243, 367120, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this an 8.  Liked the color(s) and the composition.  Difficult, but just a little sharper/more definition, especially around the head, make this even better in my opinion.</td>', 'I gave this an 8.  Liked the color(s) and the composition.  Difficult, but just a little sharper/more definition, especially around the head, make this even better in my opinion.', '2006-08-02 06:38:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687254, 367743, 37430, '<td valign="top">&gt;&gt;... the blue colour gradient across the back ground<br/> <br/>This might be possible when your subject is lit by light bulb (yellow light) and the background is not lit by same light. This might confuse your camera to choose white balance for tungsten (did I spelled it right?) light and thus giving blue tinge to background.<br/> <br/>Well, you seriously don''t need to have studio for "studio shots". All you need is plain background (any wall or cloth will do) and creative lighting. All I use in my studio shots (and their are enough in my portfolio) is light from simple light bulb hanging on free cable (so that I can move it to position ogf my choice). Sometimes computer monitor can also serve as very creative and different background.<br/> <br/>Anyway, this is good try. Black on black is a difficult situation. You also need to work on placement of your subject. Check out on rule-of-thirds.<br/> <br/>Photoshop is great, but its not easy. Fiddle with Picasa before getting into local editing with photoshop. I still manage 90% (or even more) of my processing on Picasa.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-08-02 05:47:48.</i></td>', '>>... the blue colour gradient across the back ground This might be possible when your subject is lit by light bulb (yellow light) and the background is not lit by same light. This might confuse your camera to choose white balance for tungsten (did I spelled it right?) light and thus giving blue tinge to background. Well, you seriously don''t need to have studio for "studio shots". All you need is plain background (any wall or cloth will do) and creative lighting. All I use in my studio shots (and their are enough in my portfolio) is light from simple light bulb hanging on free cable (so that I can move it to position ogf my choice). Sometimes computer monitor can also serve as very creative and different background. Anyway, this is good try. Black on black is a difficult situation. You also need to work on placement of your subject. Check out on rule-of-thirds. Photoshop is great, but its not easy. Fiddle with Picasa before getting into local editing with photoshop. I still manage 90% (or even more) of my processing on Picasa.', '2006-08-02 06:46:43.000000', '2006-08-02 06:47:48.000000', 0),
(2687267, 369132, 18202, '<td valign="top">simply stunning!</td>', 'simply stunning!', '2006-08-02 06:53:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687272, 367210, 18202, '<td valign="top">love the water shapes.</td>', 'love the water shapes.', '2006-08-02 06:54:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687279, 367973, 18202, '<td valign="top">A wonderful catch.<br/>those eyes scare me for some reason</td>', 'A wonderful catch.those eyes scare me for some reason', '2006-08-02 06:56:45.000000', NULL, 0),
