(2687549, 369217, 28710, '<td valign="top">Concept wise, this is probably my fave from the challenge.<br/> <br/>Certainly merits a fave overall.<br/> <br/>A little nitpick would be the low saturation and contrast. I would prefer to see the orange a bit more like the natural color of an orange of that type. Likewise, I would like to see a bit more of that shadowing. I wonder if it might be possible to emphasize the shadow/light from the flame light and bring up the sat just a hair on the orange itself.</td>', 'Concept wise, this is probably my fave from the challenge. Certainly merits a fave overall. A little nitpick would be the low saturation and contrast. I would prefer to see the orange a bit more like the natural color of an orange of that type. Likewise, I would like to see a bit more of that shadowing. I wonder if it might be possible to emphasize the shadow/light from the flame light and bring up the sat just a hair on the orange itself.', '2006-08-02 09:16:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687553, 369882, 28710, '<td valign="top">I think this looks great because of the lighting. It creates the illusion that they are vertical, not horizontal.<br/> <br/>Good job!</td>', 'I think this looks great because of the lighting. It creates the illusion that they are vertical, not horizontal. Good job!', '2006-08-02 09:18:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687568, 367377, 28710, '<td valign="top">Great stuff with the eyes.<br/> <br/>Bit of a dark spot on the head from lighting...<br/> <br/>Did you start with your lights at 90 degrees or 120 degrees angle from each other? Maybe they need to be a tiny bit higher... ?<br/> <br/>Lighting can be really tough.<br/> <br/>I think you are definitely starting to move beyond "coming along nicely" now...<br/> <br/>Nice to shoot someone else for a change isn''t it?<br/> <br/>A nitpick would be in the strange soft appearance of the eyes. A bit of sharpening or something might give them a bit more snap... maybe. I''d try a fairly wide radius with some strong amounts masked just to the eyes on a separate layer and maybe in darken mode and play with the opacity... Just a guess.</td>', 'Great stuff with the eyes. Bit of a dark spot on the head from lighting... Did you start with your lights at 90 degrees or 120 degrees angle from each other? Maybe they need to be a tiny bit higher... ? Lighting can be really tough. I think you are definitely starting to move beyond "coming along nicely" now... Nice to shoot someone else for a change isn''t it? A nitpick would be in the strange soft appearance of the eyes. A bit of sharpening or something might give them a bit more snap... maybe. I''d try a fairly wide radius with some strong amounts masked just to the eyes on a separate layer and maybe in darken mode and play with the opacity... Just a guess.', '2006-08-02 09:24:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2687570, 369540, 28710, '<td valign="top">Way to make harsh lighting work for ya! Yeehaw!</td>', 'Way to make harsh lighting work for ya! Yeehaw!', '2006-08-02 09:26:37.000000', NULL, 0),
