(2688376, 367682, 60995, '<td valign="top">Somehow I missed this one during voting...too bad because I love it!  It is definitely one of the best amphibian pics on this site, and as a wildlife biology student I''ve looked at about all of them!  Contrary to the others'' opinoins I would not crop off the bottom 1/4.  The only thing that distracts for me is the plant on the left of the pic beside the frog, and that could be easily cloned out in Photoshop if you wanted.  <br/> <br/>Great work!</td>', 'Somehow I missed this one during voting...too bad because I love it!  It is definitely one of the best amphibian pics on this site, and as a wildlife biology student I''ve looked at about all of them!  Contrary to the others'' opinoins I would not crop off the bottom 1/4.  The only thing that distracts for me is the plant on the left of the pic beside the frog, and that could be easily cloned out in Photoshop if you wanted.   Great work!', '2006-08-02 13:04:46.000000', NULL, 0),
