(2691958, 367855, 62891, '<td valign="top">This is astonishing, I love this!  I love the water on the petals and the two cherries together, embedded in the rose petals, great added touch.  Even with color on color, it''s eye catching.  Is it odd that I find this very romantic and yet somewhat sexual.  Would look great framed above my bed.</td>', 'This is astonishing, I love this!  I love the water on the petals and the two cherries together, embedded in the rose petals, great added touch.  Even with color on color, it''s eye catching.  Is it odd that I find this very romantic and yet somewhat sexual.  Would look great framed above my bed.', '2006-08-03 12:19:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2692112, 369126, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading post - Once again - cool shot. Love the models. The colors are nice. I think for an improvement maybe if you had brightened up the jellies just a bit (maybe dodged their outlines a tad) they may have stood out a bit more. THere is always such cool detail in a jelly body that abit more processing could have brought it out. Also maybe a bit tighter crop on top (get rid of that floater that isnt as prominent) and you may have a bit better balance. Overall these are just minor. You have a good shot and really not a bad score to go with it.</td>', 'Trading post - Once again - cool shot. Love the models. The colors are nice. I think for an improvement maybe if you had brightened up the jellies just a bit (maybe dodged their outlines a tad) they may have stood out a bit more. THere is always such cool detail in a jelly body that abit more processing could have brought it out. Also maybe a bit tighter crop on top (get rid of that floater that isnt as prominent) and you may have a bit better balance. Overall these are just minor. You have a good shot and really not a bad score to go with it.', '2006-08-03 13:00:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2692170, 369877, 47274, '<td valign="top">i like this,i think it should have scored higher, i love the way you did it, its different then every one elses</td>', 'i like this,i think it should have scored higher, i love the way you did it, its different then every one elses', '2006-08-03 13:18:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2692185, 369160, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post - Nice shot and score. The colors are rich and warm and the detail is sharp and clean on the flower head. The background color is a great compliment and the composition has a good feel to it. Nice shot overall with no real complaints or suggestions from my end.</td>', 'Trading Post - Nice shot and score. The colors are rich and warm and the detail is sharp and clean on the flower head. The background color is a great compliment and the composition has a good feel to it. Nice shot overall with no real complaints or suggestions from my end.', '2006-08-03 13:23:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2692227, 366822, 60862, '<td valign="top">Here''s an example that might benefit from more "negative space."  That means not cropping so tightly.  Look at some of the results of the negative space challenges for some ideas.  Here''s one example:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=33409" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/128/thumb/33409.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/128/thumb/33409.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/128/thumb/33409.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Your image doesn''t have the same vibrant background, but do you see how the large space away from the subject gives some interest?<br/> <br/>The other main issue here is focus.  You want the marble to be sharp and the background to be soft.<br/> <br/>You also want to avoid the harsh "spotlight" effect of the lamp.  My first entry suffered from the same problem.<br/> <br/>Search Google for "light tent" to learn some things about lighting.  I''ve been experimenting with many ways to diffuse lights, like pillowcases, tissue paper, and even my hands.<br/> <br/>Putting the light to the side will not only hide its reflection but also create some drama with shadows.  Long shadows coming out the side are more interesting than short ones directly behind.  They also look deliberate.</td>', 'Here''s an example that might benefit from more "negative space."  That means not cropping so tightly.  Look at some of the results of the negative space challenges for some ideas.  Here''s one example:  Your image doesn''t have the same vibrant background, but do you see how the large space away from the subject gives some interest? The other main issue here is focus.  You want the marble to be sharp and the background to be soft. You also want to avoid the harsh "spotlight" effect of the lamp.  My first entry suffered from the same problem. Search Google for "light tent" to learn some things about lighting.  I''ve been experimenting with many ways to diffuse lights, like pillowcases, tissue paper, and even my hands. Putting the light to the side will not only hide its reflection but also create some drama with shadows.  Long shadows coming out the side are more interesting than short ones directly behind.  They also look deliberate.', '2006-08-03 13:34:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2692363, 367111, 60862, '<td valign="top">I voted this a 9.  To me, the background was the grass.  Perfect focus, great composition.</td>', 'I voted this a 9.  To me, the background was the grass.  Perfect focus, great composition.', '2006-08-03 14:31:07.000000', NULL, 0),
